# Environment variables

Configuration is read exclusively from environment variables. Defaults below are the application defaults. The deployed values are set per environment in the product's gitops-app repo (`services.yaml` → `env`, `replicas`, `resources`).

## Core

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | `{{ port }}` | HTTP port (`server.port`). |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Root log level (`logging.level.root`). |
| `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` | `-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75` | JVM flags; keeps the heap inside the container memory limit. |
{%- if needs_observability %}

## Observability

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED` | `true` (image default) | Set to `false` to enable the OpenTelemetry Java agent. |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | _(unset)_ | OTLP endpoint traces are exported to (required when the agent is enabled). |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | `{{ project_name }}` | Service name reported in traces. |
{%- endif %}

## Build / CI

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `NVD_API_KEY` | Optional NVD API key for `devbox run audit`. Set it (as a CI secret) to use OWASP Dependency-Check; unset, `audit` falls back to `trivy fs`. |
